WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.002
And we have some breaking

00:00:02.002 --> 00:00:02.669
news for you now.

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:03.069
The U.S.

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:03.737
Supreme Court

00:00:03.737 --> 00:00:05.372
has temporarily granted

00:00:05.372 --> 00:00:07.340
a request from Republican governors

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:08.508
to keep in place

00:00:08.508 --> 00:00:09.242
the Trump era

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:12.245
pandemic border rule known as Title 42.

00:00:12.245 --> 00:00:13.213
It allows the U.S.

00:00:13.213 --> 00:00:16.383
government to push back asylum seekers

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:17.884
out of the country

00:00:17.884 --> 00:00:19.085
because of the pandemic.

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:21.287
That policy was set to expire

00:00:21.287 --> 00:00:22.022
on Wednesday.

00:00:22.022 --> 00:00:24.090
And CNN's Jessica Schneider joins us

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:24.624
live now.

00:00:24.624 --> 00:00:26.292
Jessica, tell us more about the decision.

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:26.793
Yeah, Jake,

00:00:26.793 --> 00:00:28.962
so the Supreme Court just acting here

00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:30.130
and because of it,

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:32.966
it looks like title 42 will not end

00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:35.168
as was anticipated on Wednesday.

00:00:35.168 --> 00:00:35.869
This has really been

00:00:35.869 --> 00:00:37.604
a complicated maneuvering

00:00:37.604 --> 00:00:38.671
through various courts

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:40.540
over the past few days and weeks.

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:42.175
What the Supreme Court is saying here

00:00:42.175 --> 00:00:43.309
is they're saying that, yes,

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:44.711
we will

00:00:44.711 --> 00:00:47.313
grant the REPUBLICAN-LED states request

00:00:47.313 --> 00:00:48.948
that we put the ending

00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:50.917
of this program on pause for now.

00:00:50.917 --> 00:00:53.153
So it will not end on Wednesday

00:00:53.153 --> 00:00:54.421
as originally planned.

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:55.688
However, this is really just

00:00:55.688 --> 00:00:57.090
temporary relief here.

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:58.625
What the Supreme Court is saying

00:00:58.625 --> 00:00:59.959
is that they want to hear from

00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:00.960
both parties,

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.295
the REPUBLICAN-LED states

00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:03.530
as well as the ACLU.

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:05.198
They want more briefing on this

00:01:05.198 --> 00:01:06.199
and then they'll decide

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:08.168
definitively in the coming days

00:01:08.168 --> 00:01:09.335
what to do here.

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:10.303
But right now,

00:01:10.303 --> 00:01:12.472
the Supreme Court putting the brakes

00:01:12.472 --> 00:01:14.441
on the end of this program.

00:01:14.441 --> 00:01:15.375
Now, this is a fight

00:01:15.375 --> 00:01:16.709
that has been all over,

00:01:16.709 --> 00:01:18.578
bouncing all over several courts.

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:20.647
It was just Friday night, however,

00:01:20.647 --> 00:01:21.314
that the U.S.

00:01:21.314 --> 00:01:22.916
Court of Appeals here in D.C.

00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:24.050
stepped in and said,

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:25.718
hey, republican-led states,

00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:26.786
we're not going to let

00:01:26.786 --> 00:01:27.921
you interfere in this.

00:01:27.921 --> 00:01:29.789
You can't step in to try to stop

00:01:29.789 --> 00:01:32.325
Title 42 from going away.

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:33.893
Those REPUBLICAN-LED states, though,

00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:35.962
they moved quickly to the Supreme Court.

00:01:35.962 --> 00:01:37.530
They filed today

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:38.898
and the Supreme Court acting

00:01:38.898 --> 00:01:41.034
just as quickly in the past few minutes

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:42.035
saying, yes,

00:01:42.035 --> 00:01:42.902
we will agree

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:44.037
with the REPUBLICAN-LED states.

00:01:44.037 --> 00:01:45.305
We will put this on hold

00:01:45.305 --> 00:01:47.340
for right now as this plays out.

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:48.074
So Jake,

00:01:48.074 --> 00:01:49.742
this is an incremental victory

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:50.944
for REPUBLICAN-LED states.

00:01:50.944 --> 00:01:53.379
It is not the final say on this issue.

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:55.081
However, it does give

00:01:55.081 --> 00:01:56.449
those REPUBLICAN-LED states

00:01:56.449 --> 00:01:57.484
a victory here.

00:01:57.484 --> 00:01:59.953
By not ending Title 42 on Wednesday.

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:01.988
The only caveat that I'll mention here

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:02.922
is that briefings

00:02:02.922 --> 00:02:04.457
from all of these parties,

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:06.159
they're due tomorrow.

00:02:06.159 --> 00:02:08.595
So it's possible although slight,

00:02:08.795 --> 00:02:09.796
that the Supreme Court

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:11.464
could act in the coming days

00:02:11.464 --> 00:02:12.932
here before the end of the week.

00:02:12.932 --> 00:02:14.634
So right now it looks like 40

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:17.070
title 42 will not end on Wednesday.

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:18.171
But the Supreme Court

00:02:18.171 --> 00:02:19.772
could move pretty quickly here

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:20.773
and make a decision,

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:23.176
maybe to the contrary in the coming days.

00:02:23.176 --> 00:02:25.011
So we continue that ping

00:02:25.011 --> 00:02:26.646
pong of the court system right now

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:28.381
with the Supreme Court stepping in

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:29.449
just minutes ago, Jake.

00:02:29.449 --> 00:02:31.117
So I know you can't predict, but

00:02:32.152 --> 00:02:32.719
tell us,

00:02:32.719 --> 00:02:33.620
what's your assessment

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:35.255
about what might happen next?

00:02:35.255 --> 00:02:36.556
What are the possibilities

00:02:36.556 --> 00:02:36.789
Well,

00:02:36.789 --> 00:02:38.291
it seems like the mere fact

00:02:38.291 --> 00:02:39.759
that they're stepping in here

00:02:39.759 --> 00:02:41.661
and allowing this temporary injunction

00:02:41.661 --> 00:02:42.896
to take hold, siding

00:02:42.896 --> 00:02:44.130
with the REPUBLICAN-LED states

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:45.231
here, it's

00:02:45.231 --> 00:02:47.167
possible that they might grant

00:02:47.167 --> 00:02:48.968
this emergency application

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:50.570
effectively putting title

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:53.473
40 to the end of it on pause

00:02:53.473 --> 00:02:54.574
for quite some time.

00:02:54.574 --> 00:02:56.309
So the REPUBLICAN-LED states could end up

00:02:56.309 --> 00:02:58.478
having a significant victory here

00:02:58.478 --> 00:02:59.512
because the Supreme Court

00:02:59.512 --> 00:03:01.681
could be poised to step in,

00:03:01.948 --> 00:03:04.083
maybe take up this emergency appeal.

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:05.652
Kick the can down the road.

00:03:05.652 --> 00:03:07.754
So Title 42 stays in place.

00:03:07.754 --> 00:03:09.088
More than just this week,

00:03:09.088 --> 00:03:10.323
maybe more than just this month

00:03:10.323 --> 00:03:11.558
into next year.

00:03:11.558 --> 00:03:13.359
It appears that the Supreme Court

00:03:13.359 --> 00:03:15.361
could potentially side with Republican

00:03:15.361 --> 00:03:15.929
led states

00:03:15.929 --> 00:03:17.931
as they sort of have done in this interim

00:03:17.931 --> 00:03:18.932
order here Jake.

00:03:18.932 --> 00:03:19.365
All right.

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:21.734
I want to bring in CNN's Ed Lavandera

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:22.635
into the conversation.

00:03:22.635 --> 00:03:24.103
Ed, you're at the border,

00:03:24.103 --> 00:03:26.005
and this is a humanitarian crisis

00:03:26.005 --> 00:03:27.140
you've been describing for weeks.

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:29.442
Shelters are already overflowing.

00:03:29.876 --> 00:03:31.844
Do you think the Supreme Court

00:03:31.844 --> 00:03:33.513
keeping title 42 in place,

00:03:33.513 --> 00:03:34.547
at least for now,

00:03:34.547 --> 00:03:35.949
will have any impact

00:03:35.949 --> 00:03:37.016
on what's going on there?

00:03:39.586 --> 00:03:41.221
Well, there are still

00:03:41.221 --> 00:03:43.523
a steady flow of people crossing

00:03:43.723 --> 00:03:45.091
the border

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:45.758
regardless of

00:03:45.758 --> 00:03:48.061
what is going on with Title 42.

00:03:48.061 --> 00:03:50.797
So on this side, there are still a

00:03:51.364 --> 00:03:52.098
large sized

00:03:52.098 --> 00:03:54.100
number of people here in the El Paso area

00:03:54.367 --> 00:03:56.469
who are still being released.

00:03:56.502 --> 00:03:58.471
So that doesn't really weaken

00:03:58.471 --> 00:04:00.373
the pressure on the

00:04:00.373 --> 00:04:01.975
shelters and the churches

00:04:01.975 --> 00:04:02.742
that have been housing

00:04:02.742 --> 00:04:04.110
many of these migrants

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:05.378
here in the El Paso area.

00:04:05.378 --> 00:04:07.680
But, Jake, as this news was breaking

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:09.048
I was literally in the middle

00:04:09.048 --> 00:04:10.350
of an interview

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:12.452
with a gentleman named Ruben Garcia.

00:04:12.452 --> 00:04:12.986
And Ruben

00:04:12.986 --> 00:04:15.888
is one of the if not the most well known

00:04:16.923 --> 00:04:18.124
advocate for migrants

00:04:18.124 --> 00:04:19.826
here in the El Paso area.

00:04:19.826 --> 00:04:22.228
He has worked for decades and runs

00:04:22.729 --> 00:04:24.964
a shelter called the Annunciation House.

00:04:24.964 --> 00:04:26.132
He is the

00:04:27.333 --> 00:04:28.334
most prominent

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:29.969
person involved in helping migrants

00:04:29.969 --> 00:04:31.971
and an advocate for the shelters

00:04:31.971 --> 00:04:33.373
and the churches here

00:04:33.373 --> 00:04:34.741
in the El Paso area.

00:04:34.741 --> 00:04:36.909
And as we sat down to do the interview,

00:04:37.644 --> 00:04:38.411
we were

00:04:38.878 --> 00:04:39.746
essentially giving him

00:04:39.746 --> 00:04:40.580
the breaking news about

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:41.514
what was happening.

00:04:41.514 --> 00:04:43.816
And his reaction was simply this.

00:04:43.816 --> 00:04:44.584
He's like

00:04:44.584 --> 00:04:45.885
they have known for a month

00:04:45.885 --> 00:04:47.220
that this judge had ordered this

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:48.454
all of this last minute.

00:04:48.454 --> 00:04:50.323
So you can really sense

00:04:50.323 --> 00:04:51.891
this sense of frustration

00:04:51.891 --> 00:04:53.559
and exasperation

00:04:53.559 --> 00:04:55.194
that so many leaders in Washington

00:04:55.194 --> 00:04:56.029
have had time

00:04:56.029 --> 00:04:57.130
to figure out what to do

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:58.031
with all of this.

00:04:58.031 --> 00:04:58.965
But all of this

00:04:58.965 --> 00:05:00.066
always seemingly

00:05:00.066 --> 00:05:00.933
coming down

00:05:00.933 --> 00:05:03.303
to the very last moment in the days.

00:05:03.303 --> 00:05:04.203
And these are shelters

00:05:04.203 --> 00:05:05.905
that are trying to plan

00:05:05.905 --> 00:05:07.307
as far ahead as they can.

00:05:07.307 --> 00:05:07.774
And right now,

00:05:07.774 --> 00:05:08.941
they're just trying to keep their heads

00:05:08.941 --> 00:05:09.909
above water,

00:05:09.909 --> 00:05:11.544
waking up every day, trying to figure out

00:05:11.544 --> 00:05:13.746
how much better space and

00:05:13.746 --> 00:05:16.149
and shelter spaces available in the city.

00:05:16.382 --> 00:05:19.018
So all of this, once again, throwing up,

00:05:19.018 --> 00:05:20.086
throwing everything up in the air

00:05:20.086 --> 00:05:21.154
at the very last minute

00:05:21.154 --> 00:05:22.622
is very frustrating

00:05:22.622 --> 00:05:25.325
for the men and women who are doing

00:05:25.325 --> 00:05:27.460
all sorts of intense work

00:05:27.994 --> 00:05:29.195
to keep the situation here

00:05:29.195 --> 00:05:30.263
from turning into a

00:05:30.263 --> 00:05:31.531
humanitarian disaster

00:05:31.531 --> 00:05:33.566
on the streets of these border towns.

00:05:33.966 --> 00:05:34.834
All right, Ed Lavandera

00:05:34.834 --> 00:05:35.601
and Jessica Schneider

00:05:35.601 --> 00:05:36.336
with the breaking news.

00:05:36.336 --> 00:05:36.969
Thank you so much.

